# text_en = Rajiv Gandhi gave an idea of the stature of the party at the 1985 Bombay Congress session and also in July 1987 when news of the suspension of Arun Nehru, Arif Khan and Vidyacharan Shukla from the party was received on Doordarshan by party general secretary Moopanar himself.
