# sent_id = hin-w-media-lot18at_P2_S10
# text = इस संग्रहके पहले फ्लैपपर एक कविता छपी है, जो इस प्रकार है-- हमारे हाथमें/सोनेकी नहीं/ सरकण्डेकी कलम है/ सरकण्डेकी कलम/खूबसूरत नहीं, सही लिखतीहै/ विरोधके मंच लिखतीहै/ प्रशस्तिपत्र नहीं लिखतीहै/ हम कटघरेमें खड़े हैं, खड़े रहेंगे/ और कटघरेमें खड़े हर उठे हुए हाथको/ अपने हाथमें ले लेंगे/ राजा कौरव हों या पाण्डव/ हम तो सदा बनवास झेलेंगे।
# translit_iast = isa saṃgrahake pahale phlaipapara eka kavitā chapī hai, jo isa prakāra hai-- hamāre hāthameṃ/sonekī nahīṃ/ sarakaṇḍekī kalama hai/ sarakaṇḍekī kalama/khūbasūrata nahīṃ, sahī likhatīhai/ virodhake maṃca likhatīhai/ praśastipatra nahīṃ likhatīhai/ hama kaṭagharemeṃ khar̤e haiṃ, khar̤e raheṃge/ aura kaṭagharemeṃ khar̤e hara uṭhe hue hāthako/ apane hāthameṃ le leṃge/ rājā kaurava hoṃ yā pāṇḍava/ hama to sadā banavāsa jheleṃge|
# translit_itrans = isa saMgrahake pahale phlaipapara eka kavitA ChapI hai, jo isa prakAra hai-- hamAre hAthameM/sonekI nahIM/ sarakaNDekI kalama hai/ sarakaNDekI kalama/khUbasUrata nahIM, sahI likhatIhai/ virodhake maMcha likhatIhai/ prashastipatra nahIM likhatIhai/ hama kaTagharemeM kha.De haiM, kha.De raheMge/ aura kaTagharemeM kha.De hara uThe hue hAthako/ apane hAthameM le leMge/ rAjA kaurava hoM yA pANDava/ hama to sadA banavAsa jheleMge|
# translit_indicxlit = iss sangrahake pehle flapper ack kavita chhapi hai, zoo iss prakaar hai-- hamare haathamen/soneki nahin/ sarkandeki kalam hai/ sarkandeki kalam/khubsurat nahin, sahi likhtihai/ virodhke munch likhtihai/ prashastipatra nahin likhtihai/ humm katgharemein khade hain, khade rahenge/ aur katgharemein khade hear uthhe hue hathko/ apane haathamen lay lenge/ raja kaurav hone yaa pandav/ humm too sadaa banwas jhelenge.
# text_en = The first flap of this collection has a poem printed on it which reads as follows : In our hands / Not of gold / Is a reed pen / Is a reed pen / Is not beautiful / Writes the right letter / Writes the platform of protest / Does not write the citation / We stand in the line / And will take every raised hand in the line / In our hands / Be it the kings Kauravas or Pandavas / We shall endure forever.
