# sent_id = hin-w-media-lot18at_P2_S31
# text = गाँवके प्रति उसके मनमें गहरा लगाव है-- मैंने देखा-- वह शरद्में निथरी हुई मेरे गांवकी नदी है वह रातभर झरते हुए हरसिंगारके फूलोंकी लय है वह अलगनीपर फैली मक्केकी बालियोंका रंग लेकर गुनगुनाती धूप है वह कीचड़ और रेत फसलों और घासोंके बीचसे अल्हड़ किशोरीकी तरह चली जाती हुई गाँवकी पगडंडी है गाँवके साथ उसका लगाव न तो नॉटस्टैल्जिया है और न ही गांवको आदर्श मानकर चलनेकी प्रवृत्ति।
# translit_iast = gā~vake prati usake manameṃ gaharā lagāva hai-- maiṃne dekhā-- vaha śaradmeṃ nitharī huī mere gāṃvakī nadī hai vaha rātabhara jharate hue harasiṃgārake phūloṃkī laya hai vaha alaganīpara phailī makkekī bāliyoṃkā raṃga lekara gunagunātī dhūpa hai vaha kīcar̤a aura reta phasaloṃ aura ghāsoṃke bīcase alhar̤a kiśorīkī taraha calī jātī huī gā~vakī pagaḍaṃḍī hai gā~vake sātha usakā lagāva na to naॉṭasṭailjiyā hai aura na hī gāṃvako ādarśa mānakara calanekī pravṛtti|
# translit_itrans = gA.Nvake prati usake manameM gaharA lagAva hai-- maiMne dekhA-- vaha sharadmeM nitharI huI mere gAMvakI nadI hai vaha rAtabhara jharate hue harasiMgArake phUloMkI laya hai vaha alaganIpara phailI makkekI bAliyoMkA raMga lekara gunagunAtI dhUpa hai vaha kIcha.Da aura reta phasaloM aura ghAsoMke bIchase alha.Da kishorIkI taraha chalI jAtI huI gA.NvakI pagaDaMDI hai gA.Nvake sAtha usakA lagAva na to naॉTasTailjiyA hai aura na hI gAMvako Adarsha mAnakara chalanekI pravRRitti|
# translit_indicxlit = gaanvke prati usake manmein gahara lagaav hai-- maine dekhaa-- wah sharadmen nithri hui mere gaonki nadee hai wah ratbhar jharate hue harsingarke phoolonki lay hai wah alagnipar faili makkeki baliyonka rung lakers gungunati dhoop hai wah keechad aur reit fasalon aur ghasonke beechse alhad kishoriki tarah chully jaati hui gaanvaki pagadandi hai gaanvke saath uska lagaav naa too notstalgia hai aur naa hee gaonko adarsh mankar chalneki pravritti.
# text_en = He has a deep attachment to the village -- I saw it -- it is the river of my village, asleep in the autumn, it is the rhythm of the flowers of the spring that fall at night, it is the sunshine that hums with the color of the maize fields spread over the alley, it is the mud and sand that runs like a teenager through the crops and grasses, it is the village trail. His attachment to the village is neither nostalgia nor a tendency to idealize the village.
