# sent_id = hin-w-media-lot19ba.txt_P2_S66
# text = वह ऐसी महिला लगती है जो टूटने से इनकार करती है, जो जरा भी किसी दूसरे पर झूली कि उसकी कांति धुमिल पड़ी. . . और सुनंदा को स्वयं यह अहसास हो जाता है, उसी वक्त. अलीगढ़ जैसे छोटे से कस्बे में जहां आदमी-औरत के संबंध को अब भी दकियानूसी नजर से देखा जाता है, वहां सत्येंद्र की एक प्यास बराबर बनी रही--- कोई मिला दोस्त हो. . . जिसमें पढ़े-लिखे समझदार साथी का सुख और नारी के लिए सहज प्यार दोनों एक साथ सुलभ हों.
# translit_iast = vaha aisī mahilā lagatī hai jo ṭūṭane se inakāra karatī hai, jo jarā bhī kisī dūsare para jhūlī ki usakī kāṃti dhumila par̤ī. . . aura sunaṃdā ko svayaṃ yaha ahasāsa ho jātā hai, usī vakta. alīgar̤ha jaise choṭe se kasbe meṃ jahāṃ ādamī-aurata ke saṃbaṃdha ko aba bhī dakiyānūsī najara se dekhā jātā hai, vahāṃ satyeṃdra kī eka pyāsa barābara banī rahī--- koī milā dosta ho. . . jisameṃ par̤he-likhe samajhadāra sāthī kā sukha aura nārī ke lie sahaja pyāra donoṃ eka sātha sulabha hoṃ.
# translit_itrans = vaha aisI mahilA lagatI hai jo TUTane se inakAra karatI hai, jo jarA bhI kisI dUsare para jhUlI ki usakI kAMti dhumila pa.DI. . . aura sunaMdA ko svayaM yaha ahasAsa ho jAtA hai, usI vakta. alIga.Dha jaise ChoTe se kasbe meM jahAM AdamI-aurata ke saMbaMdha ko aba bhI dakiyAnUsI najara se dekhA jAtA hai, vahAM satyeMdra kI eka pyAsa barAbara banI rahI--- koI milA dosta ho. . . jisameM pa.Dhe-likhe samajhadAra sAthI kA sukha aura nArI ke lie sahaja pyAra donoM eka sAtha sulabha hoM.
# translit_indicxlit = wah aisee mahila lagati hai zoo tootane say incar karati hai, zoo zara bhi kissy dusare para jhooli kii usaki kanti dhumil padi. . . aur sunanda coo swayam yeah ahsas how jaataa hai, usee vakt. aligarh jaise chhote say kasbe mein jahaan aadmi-aurat key sambandh coo ab bhi dakianusi nazar say dekhaa jaataa hai, vahan satyendra key ack pyaas barabar bunny rahee--- koi milaa dost how. . . jisamen padhe-likhe samajhdaar saathi kaa sukh aur naari key lie sahaj pyaar dono ack saath sulabh hone.
# text_en = She seems to be the woman who refuses to break up and who swings at anyone else to make her light fade... and Sunanda herself realizes this at the same time.In a small town like Aligarh where man-woman relations are still looked down upon, Satyendra's one thirst remained the same---to have a friend who is accessible to both the pleasure of an educated, understanding partner and the innate love of a woman.
